 "description": "One company's latest nightly StockLens score: the composite score (0 to 100) and its rating word, the domain scores with their grade words, the named signals that most shaped the reading (up to three, each with its evidence), the business-model lens where one applies, and any domain that was not scored in it. Use the rating word for the company and grade words only for a domain. A higher Risk score means a stronger risk posture and less downside concern. Without an account, scores answer for the 600 largest companies by market value; a signed-in account also reaches any company in its own portfolios. A result with a status other than scored is an answer, not an error; do not retry it unchanged. Relay its message; not_in_surface means the company is scored and outside the caller's reach, never that StockLens has no analysis. Then act on next_step: for ask_user, ask the person and call the named tool only if they agree; mention an offer on a scored result at most once per conversation. Every result carries freshness; a stale result is StockLens's last computed reading for that listing, not last night's, and should be quoted with its date. When freshness.requested_ticker is present, say which listing was served and what was asked. One ticker per call. It does not rank, sort or list companies: for any top, best, worst or filtered request call discover_stocks, and never build a ranking from repeated calls.",
